WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.972
Text columns often contain hidden inconsistencies.

00:00:03.972 --> 00:00:13.502
Extra spaces, inconsistent capitalization, abbreviations, and spelling differences can create categories that appear

00:00:13.502 --> 00:00:16.032
different even when they mean the same thing.

00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:23.647
In the example, the Pandas string accessor is used to strip spaces and convert text to lowercase.

00:00:23.647 --> 00:00:34.522
After standardization, values such as Web, web with spaces, and uppercase WEB all become one consistent category.

00:00:34.522 --> 00:00:40.822
This matters because category counts, group summaries, charts, and models all depend on consistent labels.

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:49.928
A small text-cleaning step can prevent several incorrect categories from appearing later in the analysis.
